<title>USA: TABLE-Cyprus Amax Q2 EPS $0.51 before items.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Cyprus Amax Q2 EPS $0.51 before items.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>CYPRUS AMAX MINERALS CO</p>
<p>				3 Mos ended 6/30  6 Mos ended 6/30</p>
<p>				   1997   1996	1997     1996</p>
<p>  Revenue		    $842   $740    $1,729   $1,424</p>
<p>  Costs and Expenses	718    656     1,508    1,244</p>
<p>  Income From Operations  124     84	 221	180</p>
<p>  Net Income		   66     53	 123	115</p>
<p>  Preferred Stock Dividend (5)    (5)	 (9)	(9)</p>
<p>  Net after pfd divs	$61    $48	$114     $106</p>
<p>  EPS:  Primary	    $0.65    $0.52     $1.21   $ 1.13</p>
<p>     Fully Diluted	 $0.65*   $0.52*    $1.21*   $1.13*</p>
<p>* Fully diluted EPS less than 3 percent dilutive.</p>
<p>Wgtd shrs: Primary	  93.4   93.2	93.4     93.2</p>
<p>     Fully Diluted	 103.1  102.9     103.1    102.9</p>
<p>		 (In Millions, Except Per Share Data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q2 1997 includes $0.19 a share gain on sale of Kubaka mine and $0.05 charge for the costs of a tender for debt.</p>
<p>Excluding the items, Q2 1997 EPS $0.51 a share.</p>
<p>Analyst consensus for the quarter was $0.47 per share, according to First Call.</p>
